.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-admin-payouts - Every account's payouts, read-only (lists when run bare)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 admin payouts [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the payouts of every account, newest first: each with its account, destination,
amount, status and, when it failed, why (error_code, error_reason).

.PP
Read-only: every payout write is the destination wallet's own, and the gateway holds no
funds. With the payouts feature off on this gateway the command answers 404
('rail0 admin config payouts' says whether it is on).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--account\fP=""
	Only this account's payouts (account id)

.PP
\fB--chain\fP=
	Only payouts on this chain: a slug (arc, base, …) or a chain id; the environment's gateway decides testnet vs mainnet

.PP
\fB--created-from\fP=""
	Only payouts created at/after this ISO-8601 time

.PP
\fB--created-to\fP=""
	Only payouts created at/before this ISO-8601 time

.PP
\fB--destination\fP=""
	Only payouts to this destination (destination id)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for payouts

.PP
\fB--page\fP=0
	Page number (1-based)

.PP
\fB--per-page\fP=0
	Payouts per page (max 100)

.PP
\fB--purpose\fP=""
	Filter by purpose: payout or proof

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	Sort fields (e.g. -created_at)

.PP
\fB--status\fP=[]
	Filter by status (pending, submitted, confirmed, failed); repeat or comma-separate for any of several

.PP
\fB--wallet\fP=""
	Only payouts from this wallet (wallet id)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 admin payouts --status failed --pretty
  rail0 admin payouts --account 019e748b-… --created-from 2026-11-01T00:00:00Z
  rail0 admin payouts get 01a3f0c2-…
  rail0 admin payouts events 01a3f0c2-…
  rail0 admin payouts destinations --status unverified
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-admin(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-payouts-destinations(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-payouts-events(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-payouts-get(1)\fP
